# ExerciseOnly — front-end environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for local dev. In production these are set in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables), NOT committed.
#
# Use SEPARATE Supabase projects for staging and production. Pointing a staging
# deploy at the production database is how real members' bookings get wiped by a
# test run.

# ---- Supabase ----
# Project → Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# The PUBLISHABLE / anon key. Safe to ship in the front-end — Row-Level Security is
# what protects the data.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here. Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the
# JavaScript bundle and is readable by anyone who opens devtools. The service_role
# key bypasses RLS entirely and belongs only in Supabase edge function secrets.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key

# ---- Demo mode ----
# "true" keeps the four one-tap demo logins (Sam / Dylan / Danny / Admin) on the
# login screen so Danny can still present the app without a phone signal.
# Set to "false" for the production deploy.
VITE_DEMO_LOGINS=true

# ---- PayNow ----
# Your UEN as registered with ACRA / PayNow. Shown under the static QR placeholder.
# In production this will be replaced by a real HitPay payment QR — but this must
# be set before go-live so the placeholder at least shows the correct UEN.
# Example: VITE_PAYNOW_UEN=202412345A
VITE_PAYNOW_UEN=
